      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "UNRWA USA exhibits a strong track record of scaling its impact during crises. Between 2022 and 2024, the organization achieved a <cite id=\"12\">3-year revenue CAGR of 206.6%</cite>, reflecting a massive surge in donor trust and operational capacity. This growth is supported by <cite id=\"13\">3.9 months of working capital</cite>, providing a resilient financial cushion for emergency responses. Their governance is equally robust, led by a <cite id=\"14\">13-member board of directors</cite> and a leadership team that maintains <cite id=\"15\">perfect scores in leadership and culture</cite> beacons."
      ],
      "summary": "UNRWA USA National Committee serves as a vital lifeline for Palestine refugees, focusing on education, healthcare, and emergency relief. In FY2024, the organization demonstrated remarkable growth, reporting <cite id=\"1\">$51,495,126 in total revenue</cite> to support its mission. The charity operates with exceptional fiscal discipline, maintaining a <cite id=\"2\">93.4% program expense ratio</cite> according to recent filings. This ensures that donor contributions are directed almost entirely toward services like <cite id=\"3\">food parcels, mental health support, and university scholarships</cite>. The organization is highly efficient in its resource mobilization, spending only <cite id=\"4\">$0.05 to raise every $1</cite>. Beyond financial metrics, the charity provides a <cite id=\"5\">documented theory of change</cite> that addresses the long-term thriving of refugees in Gaza, the West Bank, and Lebanon. Their work is particularly critical in Gaza, where they provide <cite id=\"6\">emergency food assistance and shelter repair</cite>. As a <cite id=\"7\">Zakat-eligible organization</cite>, it offers a verified pathway for Muslim donors to fulfill their religious obligations through a <cite id=\"8\">Platinum-rated nonprofit</cite>.",
